--TEST--
Core\IO::lines refuses an ungranted path exactly as ::read does, naming `fs.read` for the same path, counted over a sweep of a file that is on disk, a name nothing could be at and a directory — and the `foreach` never begins, so a file's line count is no more learnable without the grant than its contents are — `rule:security/capability-question-is-grant-and-scope` and `rule:security/capability-check-at-the-door`, spec § 14
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `lines` performs the whole read behind one door and only then splits, so the
// thing this case pins is an ordering: with nothing granted, the three paths
// have to become indistinguishable, and a member that opened the file to count
// its lines before asking would answer differently for the one that is really
// there.
//
// The agreement with `read` is the other half. They share `slurp`, so a
// refusal that differed between them could only mean one of the two had grown
// a door of its own.
// `Here::path` returns a literal resolved from this file's folder, and each
// name below is joined onto it, so the door is handed an absolute path.
class Here {
    public static function path(#[Core\Path] string $path): string {
        return $path;
    }
}
string $dir = Here::path('.');
array<string> $paths = [
    "note.txt",
    "no-such-dir/no-such-file.txt",
    ".",
];
int $total = Core\Arr::count($paths) as int;

int $refused = 0;
int $namingFsRead = 0;
int $linesSeen = 0;

int $i = 0;
for (; $i < $total; $i = $i + 1) {
    string $path = Core\Path::join($dir, $paths[$i]);
    string $needs = " needs the capability `fs.read` for " . $path . ", which is not granted\nhelp: grant it in nvs.toml under `[capabilities.fs]`";

    try {
        string $raw = Core\IO::read($path);
        echo "read answered for ", $path, "\n";
    } catch (RuntimeError $denied) {
        $refused = $refused + 1;
        if ($denied->message == "Core\\IO::read" . $needs) {
            $namingFsRead = $namingFsRead + 1;
        }
    }

    try {
        foreach (Core\IO::lines($path) as string $line) {
            $linesSeen = $linesSeen + 1;
        }
        echo "lines answered for ", $path, "\n";
    } catch (RuntimeError $denied) {
        $refused = $refused + 1;
        if ($denied->message == "Core\\IO::lines" . $needs) {
            $namingFsRead = $namingFsRead + 1;
        }
    }
}

echo "paths: ", $total as string, "\n";
echo "refused: ", $refused as string, "\n";
echo "naming fs.read: ", $namingFsRead as string, "\n";
echo "lines seen: ", $linesSeen as string, "\n";
--FILE note.txt--
one
two
three
--EXPECT--
paths: 3
refused: 6
naming fs.read: 6
lines seen: 0
